        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical initialization sets 0x1000, but the setter changes the quantum. Low service uses that variable, arms its callback in the final branch, and interrupt scheduling gives high-priority work precedence. This corrects the fixed-size claim without changing supported transfer semantics."
